         dict(h="Structural trailing", kicker="39.2"),
         dict(p="A structural trail moves the stop only when *structure* moves: after a new higher low forms for a long, place the stop below it. That is different from trailing by a fixed number of pips or a fixed percentage, which has no relationship to where the idea would actually be wrong."),
         dict(p="The trade-off is that structure moves in steps, sometimes large ones. A structural trail can give back a meaningful portion of an open profit before it tightens — but it gives back *only what the structure says is still valid*, which is the whole point."),
