         dict(ans="(a) Break-even at +1R would have stopped out **14 of 30 winners** — nearly half — for a small reduction in loss size. Unless the 5 complete reversals represent very large losses, break-even is probably **hurting** expectancy. (b) Test a *partial* at +1R with the stop kept original, so that the retracement trades still have a chance; or test break-even *plus spread* at +1.5R. (c) Record for every trade: maximum favourable excursion (R), whether the stop was moved, whether it was hit, and the final R. Fifty trades give a defensible answer; ten give a story."),
