         dict(ans="(a) Spread 25 pips + slippage 2 pips = 27 pips; commission USD 0.70 on 0.10 lots = 0.7 pips equivalent (pip value USD 10 per 0.10 lots... i.e. USD 7 per lot → USD 0.70 on 0.10 lots = 0.7 pips). Total ≈ **27.7 pips**, and with a 60-pip stop that is **0.46R per trade**. (b) 40 × 0.46R = **18.4R per month** in costs. (c) The system must produce **more than +0.46R expectancy per trade** before costs just to break even — which is a demanding bar, and explains why so many *profitable-looking* strategies lose. The fix is fewer, larger trades: at a 120-pip stop the same cost is 0.23R."),
